%% Library management system: explicit business decisions for downstream agents.
%% USERS already exists: preserve its exact columns, types, nullability and defaults.
%% Never recreate, alter or drop USERS as part of a new library migration.
%% Existing USERS: serial id PK; email varchar(255) NOT NULL UNIQUE;
%% name varchar(255) NULL; created_at timestamp NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW().
%% New integer entity IDs use serial PKs. Junction PKs are composite FK pairs,
%% not generated IDs. All new FKs are NOT NULL and use ON DELETE CASCADE.
%% Every user has zero or one borrower profile; every borrower has exactly one user.
%% borrowers.user_id is UNIQUE. membership_number is a required unique library ID.
%% borrowers.is_active defaults to true; inactive borrowers cannot start new loans.
%% BOOKS represents individual physical copies, not abstract titles or editions.
%% barcode is required and unique per copy. isbn is nullable text, not unique:
%% multiple copies may share an ISBN, and some books do not have an ISBN.
%% title is required; published_year is nullable integer; withdrawn_at is nullable.
%% Books may have zero or more authors and genres, allowing uncatalogued copies.
%% An author or genre may describe zero or more copies. Use explicit junctions.
%% Author full_name is required but not unique: distinct authors can share a name.
%% Genre name is required and unique using PostgreSQL's default case-sensitive equality.
%% book_authors PK = (book_id, author_id); book_genres PK = (book_id, genre_id).
%% BORROWERS and BOOKS each have zero or more historical LOANS.
%% Each loan references exactly one borrower and exactly one physical book copy.
%% A loan is active when returned_at IS NULL; completed loans are retained.
%% Require a partial UNIQUE index on loans(book_id) WHERE returned_at IS NULL:
%% one physical copy can have at most one active loan, enforced under concurrency.
%% Borrowers may hold multiple active loans; no loan limit or fines are modelled.
%% checked_out_at defaults to NOW(); due_at is required and set explicitly at checkout.
%% returned_at is nullable. CHECK due_at > checked_out_at and
%% CHECK returned_at IS NULL OR returned_at >= checked_out_at.
%% Overdue is derived from returned_at IS NULL AND due_at < NOW(); do not store it.
%% All new timestamp columns use timestamptz; never change existing USERS timestamps.
%% New non-key columns are NOT NULL unless explicitly described as nullable above.
%% Archive borrowers via is_active and books via withdrawn_at to preserve loan history.
%% Do not hard-delete users, borrowers or books with loans during normal operations.
%% Cascading FKs are structural deletion behavior, not permission to delete history.
%% Checkout must verify active borrower and non-withdrawn book in the same transaction.
erDiagram
    USERS ||--o| BORROWERS : has
    BORROWERS ||--o{ LOANS : borrows
    BOOKS ||--o{ LOANS : loan_history
    BOOKS ||--o{ BOOK_AUTHORS : credits
    AUTHORS ||--o{ BOOK_AUTHORS : writes
    BOOKS ||--o{ BOOK_GENRES : classified_as
    GENRES ||--o{ BOOK_GENRES : categorizes

    USERS {
        integer id PK "Existing serial ID"
        varchar(255) email UK "Required"
        varchar(255) name "Nullable"
        timestamp created_at "Required; default NOW()"
    }

    BORROWERS {
        integer id PK "Generated serial ID"
        integer user_id FK, UK "Required; references users.id"
        text membership_number UK "Required library member ID"
        boolean is_active "Required; default true"
    }

    BOOKS {
        integer id PK "Generated serial ID"
        text barcode UK "Required physical copy identifier"
        text isbn "Nullable; shared across copies"
        text title "Required"
        integer published_year "Nullable"
        timestamptz withdrawn_at "Nullable; archives this copy"
    }

    AUTHORS {
        integer id PK "Generated serial ID"
        text full_name "Required; not unique"
    }

    GENRES {
        integer id PK "Generated serial ID"
        text name UK "Required; case-sensitive unique"
    }

    BOOK_AUTHORS {
        integer book_id PK, FK "References books.id"
        integer author_id PK, FK "References authors.id"
    }

    BOOK_GENRES {
        integer book_id PK, FK "References books.id"
        integer genre_id PK, FK "References genres.id"
    }

    LOANS {
        integer id PK "Generated serial ID"
        integer borrower_id FK "Required; references borrowers.id"
        integer book_id FK "Required; one active loan per copy"
        timestamptz checked_out_at "Required; default NOW()"
        timestamptz due_at "Required; after checkout"
        timestamptz returned_at "Nullable; NULL means active"
    }
